secure-eye (0.3.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Added
    - `secureEye fetch-models` downloads the three data files the dlib
      backend needs (about 28 MB) and checks them against pinned sha256
      sums. The packages can't ship them because their build services run
      offline. The Dashboard in `secure-eye-gui` has a matching "Download
      dlib data files" button. It is enabled only when `detector_backend =
      dlib` and the files are missing.
  * Changed
    - The mediapipe backend is now available on aarch64 for Ubuntu and
      Fedora: `ppa:vhrabar/tools` and `copr:vhrabar/python-extras` build
      `python3-mediapipe` for it, so `secure-eye` now depends on it on
      aarch64 as well as x86_64, and aarch64 installs no longer have to
      switch `detector_backend` to dlib.

 -- Vedran Hrabar <vedran.hrabar@outlook.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

secure-eye (0.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed
    - 0.3.1 never reached Ubuntu, Fedora or the AUR: its Debian changelog
      entry had the same date as 0.3.0's, which lintian rejects, so the
      release stopped before publishing. Releases dated the same day now get
      distinct times.

